  "body": "## v1.13.3\r\n\r\nA small follow-up to 1.13.2 to fix a couple of confusing edge cases. Quoted options could look like plain text in the editor but still affect requests; that's now fixed. I've also added a warning for trace budgets written with ==.\r\n\r\n### Quoted options\r\n\r\nThe parser used to strip the quotes from `\"timeout=1s\"` and set the timeout. It now treats that field as text, matching highlighting and completion.\r\n\r\nDirectives such as `@settings`, `@ssh`, `@k8s`, `@sse`, and `@mock` warn when an option is quoted as a whole:\r\n\r\n```http\r\n# @settings \"timeout=1s\"\r\n\r\n### Health\r\nGET {{base.url}}/health\r\n```\r\n\r\n```text\r\nWarnings:\r\n  api.http:1: @settings option \"timeout=1s\" is quoted. Write it as timeout=1s\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe warning doesn't stop the run. Other options on the same line still apply. To set the timeout, write `timeout=1s`. If a value needs spaces, quote just the value: `cmd=\"gh auth token\"`.\r\n\r\nOther directives handle these fields differently:\r\n\r\n- `@auth` rejects quoted fields where it expects options. In 1.13.2, `# @auth global command \"name=gh\" cmd=\"gh auth token\"` named the definition `gh`. It now reports a parse error and stops the run:\r\n\r\n  ```text\r\n  error[parse]: @auth expects key=value options but got \"name=gh\". Quote a value that has spaces\r\n  ```\r\n\r\n  Use `name=gh` to name the definition.\r\n\r\n- `@trace` reports an unknown option, such as `unknown @trace option \"total=1s\"`.\r\n- `@compare` and `@script` treat the quoted field as a value.\r\n\r\nThe [request file docs](https://resterm.app/docs/request-files/#separators-and-comments) list the option rules.\r\n\r\n### Trace budget typos\r\n\r\n`dns==50ms` used to be ignored silently. It now produces a warning:\r\n\r\n```http\r\n### Health\r\n# @trace dns==50ms total<=400ms\r\nGET {{base.url}}/health\r\n```\r\n\r\n```text\r\nWarnings:\r\n  api.http:2: unknown @trace option \"dns==50ms\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nUse `dns<=50ms` or `dns=50ms`.\r\n\r\n### Upgrading from 1.13.0 or earlier\r\n\r\n- [1.13.2](https://github.com/unkn0wn-root/resterm/releases/tag/v1.13.2) enforces `request_headers<=` and `request_body<=` budgets, exits with `2` on usage errors in `init`, `collection`, and `history`, and rejects `@auth apikey cookie`.\r\n- 1.13.2 also made `<=` in place of `=` an error in regular options, as in `# @settings timeout<=1s`. Only `@trace` budgets take `<=`. A file or global `@ssh` or `@k8s` profile written this way is not available to requests.\r\n"
